Syntax: junk <item>

Junk permanently destroys one item from your inventory.

In-code behavior:
- Junk only searches your carried inventory (not room contents).
- You must supply an item name; otherwise you get a prompt.
- If found, the item is extracted immediately and cannot be recovered.
- Junk gives no gold, no favor, and no alignment effect.
- If the item is not in your inventory, junk fails with an error message.

Use junk to quickly clear worthless inventory clutter.
Use sacrifice when you want gold/alignment effects from room objects/corpses.
